# This repository is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but everything under
# mudakop/ and luci-app-mudakop/root/ is executed on the router by ash. A CRLF shebang
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/ash\r", which does not
# exist, and the shell reports that as "not found". Sourced .sh files are just as
# affected: a trailing CR ends up inside variable values.
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository and check out LF everywhere, so the platform the
# checkout happens on cannot change what ships in the package.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build artefacts are binary and must never be line-ending converted
*.apk binary
*.ipk binary
